% The same evidence against the exception, but with the 0.58 on the
% PREMISE of a certain rule instead of on the rule. A rule confidence
% lowers the strength of what the rule derives. A premise confidence means
% that the premise instance is active in that fraction of activation
% worlds: with 0.58 the rule derives a certain -injured(a) and the
% exception is cancelled completely; with 0.42 the rule does not apply and
% the exception keeps its full 0.6. flies(a) is reported with
% 0.58*1 + 0.42*(1-0.6) = 0.748; bird_counter.gkp gives 0.98.
bird(a).
0.6::injured(a).
0.58::vet(a).
-injured(X) :- vet(X).
flies(X) :- bird(X), unless(injured(X), 2).
query(flies(a)).
